## Working agreements

- Run the full verification sequence above before declaring work done. Fix failures you caused; report pre-existing or environment failures separately.
- Add or update tests with every behavior change.
- Keep imports at the top of the module.
- Never commit `.env` files, credentials, tokens or generated secrets.
- This project was generated from a Copier template. Do not edit `.copier-answers.yml`; pull template improvements with `uvx copier update --trust` on a clean working tree.
{%- if agents and "context7" in mcp_servers %}
- Use the Context7 MCP server when you need current library or API documentation.
{%- endif %}
{%- if agents and "github" in mcp_servers %}
- The GitHub MCP server can write. Confirm consequential write operations (merges, releases, settings) with the user first.
{%- endif %}

## Branches and releases (GitOps)

- `main` is production and `dev` is integration{% if github_ci %}; both change only through pull requests, and `pr-policy` CI enforces the rules below{% endif %}. Never commit or push to `main`, `dev`, `qa` or `staging` directly; the git hooks refuse it.
- Work on `<github-user>/<type>/<kebab-name>` branches cut from `dev`, with type one of `feat`, `fix`, `chore`, `docs`, `refactor`, `perf`, `test`, `build`, `ci`, `style`, `revert`, `hotfix`. Example: `octocat/feat/health-check`.
- Feature PRs target `dev` and are squash-merged. `main` accepts PRs only from `dev` (or `qa`/`staging`), Dependabot and release-please, merged with a merge commit.
- PR titles and commit messages follow Conventional Commits (`feat(api): add health check`); release-please turns them into the changelog, the version bump and the GitHub release.
- Link issues in the PR body (`Closes #12`).
